WEBVTT

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.290
It's already been ten years, huh?

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.000
Sorry, Mitsuyoshi.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.620
My departure was scheduled earlier on short notice.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.580
Let's go take some pictures of trains
once I get back, okay?

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.870
Daddy!

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.410
Whoa!

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.500
You've gotta be a good girl, okay, Yui?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.870
Okay!

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.160
Well, Mitsuyoshi, Mom is going
to drop Dad off at the airport, okay?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.660
Yui and Grandpa, take care of Nyanko Big for me.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.500
Have a safe trip!

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:09.450
I'm getting older and older,
but your smiles never change.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:13.910
Grandpa doesn't change one bit either,
right, Nyanko Big?

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.750
He's gotten fatter, though.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:22.250
You were the one who named him "Nyanko Big"
so that he'd get big, weren't you, Big Bro?!

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.620
I don't remember that.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.870
Heya, Mitsuyoshi!

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.620
Hello! Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.120
Welcome!

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.950
We've been expecting you, Kaoru-kun.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.580
10 TH ANNUAL
KAORU IJUIN

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:35.080
So, what are you gonna do this year?

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.790
Dun-da-da-dah!

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:42.290
The red-letter Tenth Annual Kaoru Ijuin Show is...

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:43.750
Ta-da!

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.700
I'm going to entertain you with every luxury imaginable!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:59.700
Tada Never Falls in Love

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.080
Hey, look over here

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.500
The viewfinder is always set

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.910
If it isn't of you, then it doesn't appeal to me

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:13.080
Did something happen to me?

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.410
I walked past my friends

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.540
And my close friend, whom I keep missing

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.040
It's a turbulent world

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.450
By the time I realized it, the world was like a rainbow

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.870
Oh, seasons, stop

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:35.950
In the photos of our time together

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:41.330
Every single thing is shining brightly

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:47.410
Hey, there's one thing I want to tell you

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:54.500
I can't stop it or hide it anymore; that feeling is right here

00:02:54.500 --> 00:03:02.750
Baby, before you vanish into this film we call "memories"

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.540
There's something I want to tell you

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.290
"I'm in love with you now"

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.910
It's Okay. They Don't Exist

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:26.040
Reserved
for the Day

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:26.080
Grandpa, I'm gonna borrow your kitchen, 'kay?!

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.200
Okay, take your time.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.080
All right! Let's get cracking!

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.750
So, Ijuin-kun's "show" is a party where
we're treated to his cooking, huh?

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:41.540
He might not look like it,
but Ijuin-kun is incredibly good at cooking!

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.660
I'm surprised.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.580
Why?!

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.450
Senpai's family owns a famous, old
Japanese-style restaurant, right?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.290
Yeah!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:53.000
That's why I'm pro-level at cooking!
I mean, my cooking skills make even Iron Chefs green!

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.500
Right, Mitsuyoshi?!

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:55.870
Yeah...

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:57.410
You're green, no doubt.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.000
That's not true!

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.120
Well, the meat from last year was pretty good, I guess.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:08.290
But clouds of smoke billowed from the garden 'cause
you barbecued, and Nyanko Big got all riled up!

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.410
Meow.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.330
I saw you lose it, too, Nyanko Big!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.620
Hiss!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.620
Hiss!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.620
Whoa there!

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.120
Cats' paw pads have a lot
of pressure points, too, you know!

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.000
Meow!

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.200
A Trepid Nyanko Big update!

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.080
Meow-meow!

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.080
See you later!

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:32.290
Okay, okay, okay! Without further ado,
I'm going to make some food!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.120
Come forth, today's menu!

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.580
~Today's Menu~

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.120
Ta-da!

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.040
Here are the results from the preliminary survey
for what everyone wants to eat most right now!

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.660
Starting with Teresa-chan!

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.910
~Today's Menu~

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.830
~Natto Roll~
Teresa-chan

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:45.870
Ta-da!

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.870
Natto roll!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.080
Yes!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.290
As for Alec...

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:58.750
~Katsudon~

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:58.750
Note: Katsudon is a bowl of rice topped with a fried pork cutlet.
"Katsu" is a homonym for the verb "win."

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.370
Ta-da!

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.910
Katsudon! Katsudon!

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:58.790
Alec, do you want to beat someone
at something? Do you?

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.290
I want to beat your head in.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:06.160
And meat-lover Yamashita Dog requested steak...

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.080
Yes! Meat!

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.830
Wait, Ijuin-senpai, you're losing steam!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:17.160
~Steak~
Yamashita

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.160
It's okay.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.450
Huh? What's okay?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.040
Next! Class Rep requested...

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.450
Ta-da! Omurice!

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:20.080
~Omurice~
Class Rep

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:20.910
Wow!

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.040
I'll write your name for free.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.370
You don't have to do that for me...

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.830
~Omurice~

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.200
Pin-senpai requested...

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:35.080
~Hamburg Steak~
Pin-senpai

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:34.700
Ta-da! Hamburg steak! Hamburg steak!
Hamburg steak... uh...

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:37.540
I'll write your name for free!

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.750
You ran out of jokes, didn't you?

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:39.700
Tee-hee!

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.330
And Yui-chan requested...

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:44.250
Ta-da! Buri-daikon! Simple but refined!

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.950
Note: Buri-daikon is a dish of yellowtail and daikon simmered
with soy sauce, sugar, ginger, and onion.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:45.950
~Buri-daikon~

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.000
By contrast, Mitsuyoshi requested...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:50.200
~Curry Rice~
(Mild)

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:50.200
Mitsuyoshi

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.250
Curry! And mild curry, at that! Kiddy food!

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.620
Get off my back.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.580
Are you the Little Prince?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.330
Whatever. Just move on.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.830
Okay! So, thanks for the amazingly
diverse requests, everyone!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.330
Well, these are no problem with my skills,
so I'm gonna start cooking!

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.450
Oh, ingredients...

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:08.910
Bring it on!

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.330
Ijuin-kun is really fired up, isn't he?

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.500
He's more irritating than usual.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:18.370
Oh! Writing "irritating" in kanji sure
is difficult to write, isn't it?

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.080
Can you write it, Alec? Can you?

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.870
He's even more irritating.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.160
Note: The kanji for "rose" is difficult for Japanese people
to remember how to write.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.200
I can write "rose"!

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.160
ROSE

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.790
Shall I prune you to death?

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:30.660
Eep! Okay, everyone. Look forward to your meals!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.500
State one color of the rainbow!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.500
Eek! Uh... p-purple!

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:48.040
The color of the rainbow is rainbow! Meet your maker!

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.040
I believe they do say one color of the rainbow...

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.750
But they get executed anyway...

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.910
Always make your heart rainbow!

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.250
Meet your maker!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.750
Wow! Teresa-san, you're so powerful!

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.660
I won't lose!

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:07.540
Oh... Aw, man...

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.000
Yay!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.870
Pin-senpai, here you go!

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.910
Ugh... The color of the rainbow...

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.620
...is rainbow!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.580
You weren't able to execute him, huh?

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.080
Class Rep! Take this card!

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:24.910
No thanks.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.040
Wha-?! You traitor!

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.160
Class Rep, please tell me you're not guru
at this or something...

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:33.410
That's impossible.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:36.790
Meet your maker!

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.040
WHAT?!

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:39.830
No fair, Big Bro!

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.370
Tada!

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.120
That's Senpai for you!

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.000
Do you need help with anything?

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.870
Okay, let's go!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:46.120
Nope, I just have a little more to do, so it's okay! Thanks!

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:47.580
What about these?

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:51.160
Oh, it'd be helpful if you could put those
in the fridge upstairs to keep them cool.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.580
Got it!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.250
Take care of that one.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.870
Oh, okay!

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.450
Thanks, you two!

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.080
Then, I, too...!

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.000
NO!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.250
The game isn't over yet! Sit as you were!

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.950
It's okay, Alec.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.160
Hajime-chan, calm down. You're getting too worked up over this.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.700
Okay...

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.700
Leave it here.

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:14.580
Okay!

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.120
Oh!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.200
Meow!

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:22.450
This is where you were, Nyanko Big-san?

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:23.660
Meow!

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.950
Wow!

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.700
Are these photos of you and Yui-chan, Tada-kun?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.700
Yeah.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.580
You both were so cute!

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:35.580
Ah! You used to be this itty-bitty, huh, Nyanko Big-san?

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:36.700
Meow!

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.830
This sure is a lovely photo.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.830
Something about it is similar to
the photos you take, Tada-kun.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:54.120
Or perhaps I should say the photo
gives off a warm and fuzzy feeling.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:57.330
No one's ever told me that before.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.370
Huh?

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.790
That's the last photo my dad took of us.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:08.200
He and my mom died in an accident ten years ago.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:10.830
He took that picture of us on the morning that they left.

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:17.500
Only the camera came back intact,
and that photo was inside of it.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.540
It was ten years ago?

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:30.500
I bet you've been living your life wishing
to be stronger ever since that day.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.910
I don't know about that.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:45.450
Mitsuyoshi! Teresa-chan! Food's ready!

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:46.750
We're heading down now!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.250
Meow!

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:52.250
Wow! Looks good!

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:54.040
This is seriously amazing!

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:56.120
Let's eat!

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.120
Yeah! Eat like mad, everyone!

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:00.830
It's delicious!

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.790
Indeed!

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:04.160
How do you like it? Is it good? Is it good?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.250
Yes! This meat's the best!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.200
The yellowtail is so tender!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.330
I know, right?! It's tender!

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:15.200
This is amazing, Ijuin-kun!
You truly are amazing at cooking!

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:16.790
Yes, I am!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.700
You've got a ways to go.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:19.450
What?!

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.580
But you ate all of your food!

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:26.370
Geez, you're not very honest.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.580
So, how is it, Mitsuyoshi?

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.870
Yeah, it's good.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.700
Hnnng! Right? Right?!

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.370
I really am amazing!

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:41.450
Everyone, eat like mad! There's enough for seconds!

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.910
IJUIN

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.950
Seconds, please!

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.580
Meow!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.750
That was so good, Ijuin-senpai!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.700
It was so good that I overate!

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:52.950
I know, right?

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:56.950
But this year's Kaoru Ijuin Show goes on!

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.120
So, where are we going?

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.870
Do you really wanna know? Do you?

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:04.870
You've indeed become irritating, so out with it already.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.290
Roger!

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.950
Well, this was the long-awaited
tenth annual commemoration,

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:11.620
so I thought we'd try something totally new.

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:14.910
I'd reserved a sento for later.

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.200
You reserved a sento?!

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.370
Are you serious?!

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.120
I'm serious.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.290
Just as you'd expect, rich people
do things to the extreme.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.370
Indeed...
Yes...

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.290
"Sento"?

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:33.870
Note: The "sento" Teresa is thinking of means "battle."

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.450
Are we renting katana?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.910
No, a sento is...

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.250
a public bathhouse.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:38.870
THE Gin no Yu

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.160
Wow!

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.870
The Gin no Yu...

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:41.790
It's lovely!

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:45.160
This building looks like one that
Rainbow Shogun would appear from.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:50.330
Yeah! The building is nice,
but the baths here are the best!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.250
There's just one problem...

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:53.250
Huh?

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.620
Welcome
This sure is a nice bath Pull

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:56.750
That's a kappa, right?

00:11:55.620 --> 00:12:08.870
THE Gin no Yu

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:58.290
It's their mascot, though.

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:02.750
I guess. A real kappa isn't as nice.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.450
There is no real or fake kappa.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.620
They don't exist, after all.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.910
That's true!

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:08.950
Let's head in.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:15.500
Okay! So, let's sento, everyone!

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.330
This sure is a nice bathhouse.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.330
Yeah.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:39.370
I've actually never been to a sento before.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.830
Well, you probably wouldn't go to one, usually.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:48.120
I sometimes want to jump into a wide bath,
so I come here every now and then.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.000
I can see them! I can see them!

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:51.580
Huh?

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.250
The wall is transparent!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.830
Your glasses are completely fogged up, you know.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.250
Wow!

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.500
This is my first time at a bathhouse!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:02.200
Yes.

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:03.540
I'm so impressed!

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.200
Okay.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:06.500
I'm glad.

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:15.910
Do boys really love girls with big boobs?

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.370
Are you talking about Yamashita-san?

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.830
N-no!

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.870
I mean, in general!

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:26.750
Well... it wouldn't be right to think of someone
like Hajime-chan as a representation of guys.

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:33.500
Oh! But the other day, Pin-senpai also said,
"It's not about her chest size!"

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:38.160
What?! That's so true! Pin-senpai says
some nice things, doesn't he?!

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.000
Yeah!

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:43.250
You're so kind, Teresa-san!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:47.450
I'd be happy if you became my big brother's girlfriend!

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:48.250
What?!

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:51.000
Do you happen to have a boyfriend, Teresa-san?

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.620
Wh-what's gotten into you, all of a sudden?

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.120
So, do you?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.660
Um, a b-boyfriend...?

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:02.750
She has one.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.120
What?!

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.080
She has one?! Really?!

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:08.370
What's he like?! Tell me!

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:10.500
I was just kidding.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.700
What?!

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:16.790
What gives? I believed you, Alec-san! Geez!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.830
Then, how about you, Alec-san?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.410
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:21.700
No, I don't.

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:22.870
Do you have a crush?

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:24.540
No, I don't.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.000
Then, do you have a first love?

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:27.830
I haven't fallen in love yet.

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:32.120
Lies! You totally have a first love!

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:35.450
Huh?

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:41.410
I've never fallen in love, but I've read novels on it.
So, I know what it's like.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:46.120
People say that falling in love once is more important
than reading hundreds of books.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:54.450
Well, Alec has read thousands of books, so maybe that
means she's fallen in love with dozens of people!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:55.580
What?!

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:59.040
Really?! That's amazing! Come on, tell me about them!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.620
They're having fun over there.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.370
The Class Rep is laughing a lot, too.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.080
That's pretty unusual, huh?

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.000
She laughs quite a bit.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:13.620
You say that stuff, but you actually like
the Class Rep, don't you, Pin-senpai?

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:15.620
That's impossible!

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.870
So, how about you, Yamashita Dog?
Got a crush on anyone?

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:20.910
What?

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:24.660
You sorta seem like you'd go out with an older girl.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:30.120
You're pretty sharp. But it's one-sided,
so I've got no chance.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.750
Is that girl... well-endowed?!

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.870
Is she well-endowed?! Is she?!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:39.330
I don't want to say. Besides, does it
have anything to do with you, Senpai?

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.910
It does! Asking for her chest size is male etiquette!

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:46.200
Hey, didn't you say that size doesn't matter?

00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.660
The bigger, the better!

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:50.790
He's the worst.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:51.540
Hm?

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:55.540
How about you, Ijuin-senpai?

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.160
I can't belong to anyone!

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:03.120
Okay, so you don't need anyone, right?

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:05.540
I do need someone! I seriously want a girlfriend!

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:07.250
How about you, Tada-senpai?

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:07.790
Hm?

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.790
There's no way he would have a crush!

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.910
If you did, you'd ask me for advice, right?!

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:12.910
That's true.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:13.620
See?

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:16.500
What?! I want you to ask me for advice, too!

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.450
Okay.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:21.080
Pin-senpai, how long are you going to soak in there?!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:21.750
Huh?

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.910
Whoa, you look as red as an octopus!

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:25.450
I'll get out.

00:16:36.330 --> 00:16:37.250
Pin-senpai!

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:38.450
Are you okay?!

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.080
Senpai! Senpai, get ahold of yourself!

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.160
His eyes are rolled back.

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:48.160
K-k-kappa... Kappa! He lost his balance
because of the kappa!

00:16:48.120 --> 00:16:49.750
Bath Rates
Adult   480 yen
Child   200 yen (elementary student)
Child    80 yen (infant)

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.410
It would've been really dangerous if
you had banged your head in the wrong spot.

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:55.540
It's a good thing you're okay.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:56.580
Yeah...

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.120
Here.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.250
You're really stupid.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:03.830
Sorry.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:09.750
Kappa really are scary! It's this guy's fault!
This place was a kappa's lair after all!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.620
Kappa don't exist.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:12.290
What?!

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.040
There's one right here!

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.950
It stopped raining!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:20.700
Yes!
Yeah!

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:23.000
It's slippery, so watch your step.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:23.750
Okay.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.330
Kappa are so scary!

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:27.870
You okay?

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:28.910
Huh?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.870
Yeah!

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.120
So, there you have it, everyone!

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:37.370
The Tenth Annual Kaoru Ijuin Show has come to a close!

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.500
Good job, Senpai!

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.700
Yeah! We had a good meal and a nice bath!

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.160
Despite you slipping.

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:49.000
Thank you very much, Ijuin-kun! I had a lot of fun!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.290
Really?! Really?!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.040
Yes!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.120
Yeah, it was fun!

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.620
Right, Big Bro?

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:55.660
Yeah!

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.000
Great!

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.330
Welp, let's go home!

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:01.950
Yeah. Is the train station that way?

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:02.660
Yes.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.660
Ah, I feel so good!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.160
Feels different when you use a big bath, huh?

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.910
I don't know why, but I feel light on my feet.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.500
My mind even feels light!

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.200
Senpai, you were...

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.660
Hey, Mitsuyoshi.

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.660
Yeah?

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:22.160
In case you're ever about to lose your balance
because of a kappa, be sure to tell me!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:26.950
It's okay. They don't exist. Besides, that'll never happen.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:32.200
But if it did happen, you'd save me, right?

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.080
Well, it's never gonna happen, though.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.580
You don't know that!

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:45.200
You never say anything, so...

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.620
Thanks for always doing this.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.370
For doing what?

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:59.330
For the Kaoru Ijuin Show. But I'm okay now.

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:07.540
Wha- I mean, it's not like that! I know that you're okay!

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:11.040
But I'm doing this because I like to!

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:16.950
I'm gonna do this next year, the year after,
and ALL the years that follow!

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:19.750
I don't care if you ask me to stop!

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:25.750
The Kaoru Ijuin Show will go on for all eternity, got that?!

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:27.620
So, brace yourself!

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:30.000
No way!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.000
Why, you...!

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.700
Don't give me that!

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.830
Hey, stop it! I can't breathe!

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.080
What do you wanna eat next year?

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:40.830
Next year?!

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:41.370
Curry?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.040
Curry is fine!

00:19:42.040 --> 00:19:42.700
Spicy curry?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:43.500
No!

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.580
Bye-bye! Thanks, Kaoru-kun!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:51.000
Later!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.500
See you tomorrow!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:59.870
Today's the anniversary of my dad and mom's death.

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:05.290
Kaoru-kun seems to have done this
so that we wouldn't be sad.

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:08.370
So, this is the Kaoru Ijuin Show's tenth year, too.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:14.370
You know, I didn't get along with him a long time ago...

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:30.200
After the funeral, he kept pestering me every single day.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.910
Mitsuyoshi!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.290
Cheer up!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.000
Mitsuyoshi!

00:20:37.160 --> 00:20:39.660
Talk to me about anything, okay?!

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:44.290
But on the day of the first anniversary
of my parents' death...

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:45.200
Mitsuyoshi!

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:45.910
Huh?

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:50.700
Today, I'm going to invite you to
the Kaoru Ijuin Show, got that?!

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:56.370
I realized that that was his own way of being nice.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:21:00.290
Ijuin-kun really cares about you, huh, Tada-kun?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:01.910
I don't know about that.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:06.620
He's a pest, but he's got some good points, too.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:08.410
That's right, Alec-san!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.700
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.200
Okay!

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:32.500
I kept wondering how long this would last

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:43.750
I had no idea why you were so pretty that day

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:50.040
After taking you away, someone who calls himself "God"

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:55.950
Says that I will never see you again

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:01.580
Where are you going? There was nothing I could do

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:06.580
You beautiful person

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:13.080
I miss you so much

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:18.700
If one of my wishes were to come true

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:24.660
I would want to hold you tight right now

00:22:24.660 --> 00:22:30.290
I only wanted to be with you forever

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:35.500
Within my heart is a melody of a flood of tears

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:44.160
I can't ever forget the days I spent with you

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:50.750
I heard that katsudon is a dish that
is served by police in Japan.

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:54.750
Did you hear that from Rachel?
Aren't you being fooled again?

00:22:58.910 --> 00:22:59.830
Alec...?

00:23:05.750 --> 00:23:06.950
Hey, Alec!

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:10.500
Charles?! What are you doing here?

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:12.500
I came here after pursuing you.

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:19.330
The future queen of Larsenburg...

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.330
Princess Teresa de Larsenburg.

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:31.200
Tada-kun, I hear that it rains
about 100 days a year in Tokyo.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:34.620
Almost one-third of the year, huh?
We've had a lot of guerilla rainstorms recently, too.

00:23:34.620 --> 00:23:35.870
A gorilla rainstorm?!

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:36.790
It's "guerilla."

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:39.830
Next time: Episode 6, "I'm Not a Rain-bringer."

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:40.870
I'm Not a Rain-bringer

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:40.910
Please look forward to it!
